From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a process that may start none has its desktop window without a shell, and no error

Chromium's and QtWebEngine's sandboxed children run on an alternate desktop and may start no process; Wine's attempt to start an explorer for that desktop is refused (c000049d) and each child logged an error. The desktop window made afterwards with no process behind it is what Windows gives every desktop (win32k makes them), so that case is traced only.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/winstation.c
@@ -924,6 +924,16 @@
             NtClose( thread );
             NtClose( process );
         }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_SANDBOX_DESKTOP_ERR
+        /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9803): a process that may start no other process -- its child
+         * process policy restricts it (PROCESS_CREATION_CHILD_PROCESS_RESTRICTED) or its job's active
+         * process limit is reached, as for Chromium's and QtWebEngine's sandboxed renderer and GPU
+         * processes on their alternate desktop -- has its desktop window made below with no shell
+         * behind it. That is what Windows gives every desktop (win32k makes desktop windows, no process
+         * is started for them), so it is no error. */
+        else if (status == STATUS_CHILD_PROCESS_BLOCKED || status == STATUS_QUOTA_EXCEEDED)
+            TRACE_(win)( "no shell for desktop %s: this process starts no others (%x)\n", debugstr_w(desktop), status );
+#endif
         else ERR_(win)( "failed to start explorer %x\n", status );
 
         SERVER_START_REQ( get_desktop_window )
